{"kind":"event","event_id":5599,"event_uid":"01M2MCNM0TBEMD9T2A89YEZ9XS","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":260,"issue_uid":"01M2MCKD4A8G0348H62ZK9KHJ1","issue_short_id":"khj1","actor":"impl:3@run-156","hlc_physical_ms":1789538258970,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"7eec5d016c7414cb88fbaf768d491967ac571db9898ae1c4e1d6053652417253","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2MCNM0SDYPDM72WQ3PC27YR","author":"impl:3@run-156","body":"Approach: two edits. (1) fleet/sandbox-boot.sh mutant_cell(): keep the EM and SURVIVED branches first, change only the final all-killed return to yield `killed, reviewer skipped` when row.get('reviewVerdict') == 'skipped-mutant-killed', else `killed`. (2) fleet/CONTRACT.md Publish card paragraph: add one clause inside the sed range (table header line → Residuals line) naming the three mutant-cell readings in the paragraph's own register. The exam at fleet/tests/test_sandbox_boot_card_cells.mjs is peer-owned; I verify behaviour with a scratch harness outside the tree.","created_at":"2026-09-16T05:57:38.969051562Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T05:57:38.97Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":5600,"event_uid":"01M2MCNXZ9FK0ZZ5VNQPBVJK8N","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":258,"issue_uid":"01M2MCK5QTCS16QCCB1W0JXHW3","issue_short_id":"xhw3","actor":"impl:1@run-156","hlc_physical_ms":1789538269161,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"3fb0d90742f700f8b067a02f133dcb4e3428db1cdc627bd5031f63feeef58d67","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2MCNXZ7SH5RFEQKK79AVHVP","author":"impl:1@run-156","body":"Approach (task 1, reviewOnStateExams): read the switch once near the top of runEngine as `args.reviewOnStateExams === true`; add `everyMutantKilled(rows)` beside `stateExamBlock` spelling the predicate once and have `stateExamBlock` call it; put the skip in the review-round block after `editedDiffs` is bound and before the prompt is assembled, returning the same `done` row shape with `reviewVerdict: 'skipped-mutant-killed'`. The Proof's Test: path (fleet/tests/test_run_engine_review_economy.mjs) is the peer's exam, so I write no legs into it; I verify against a scratch copy of the legs under /tmp that imports the tree's helpers, then delete it. Docs: report-format.md reviewVerdict + stateExams rows, CONTRACT.md Exam environment bullet.","created_at":"2026-09-16T05:57:49.159056892Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T05:57:49.161Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":5601,"event_uid":"01M2MCPEAT5YJ5DM182TQDDF8A","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":259,"issue_uid":"01M2MCK99ZCQ1HCADKYSVK26CR","issue_short_id":"26cr","actor":"impl:2@run-156","hlc_physical_ms":1789538285914,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"556c5127cb1be1947431e56a5d0e7db98cc87c5c4a91dfa4dc03aa15880bd106","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2MCPEAS4A9SAW3YM427Y2ZK","author":"impl:2@run-156","body":"Both deletions landed as two single hunks, deletion-only.\n\nexaminer.md rule 2: dropped the clause ` — one that would pass against a stub is not that leg`. Note for a later session: `live.` could not stay on its own continuation line. Leg (a) folds rule 2 with `tr '\\n' ' '`, which preserves the 3-space indent, so `check\\n   live.` folds to `check    live.` and the grep for `keep that check live.` misses. The two lines had to collapse into one 82-char line — already the file's existing max width, so no re-wrap of the surrounding lines was needed and the hunk stays at one `+` line for M3.\n\nreviewer.md rule 5: dropped the sentence `A test that still passes with the behavior it names deleted is a finding, blocking when it leaves a criterion unverified.`; rule 5 now ends `tests asserting observable behavior.` on the line that already carried it, one `+` line.\n\nAll five Run: legs and the Check: are green. wc -w now 894 (was 906) and 1500 (was 1521) — deletion-only, as the Context predicted. The amendment-lens sim still prints ALL TESTS PASSED on the edited reviewer.md. Rollback of the experiment is a revert of exactly these two hunks.","created_at":"2026-09-16T05:58:05.913077213Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T05:58:05.914Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":5602,"event_uid":"01M2MCQ1ZBCK4A4DJ5YWK5H32B","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":260,"issue_uid":"01M2MCKD4A8G0348H62ZK9KHJ1","issue_short_id":"khj1","actor":"exam:3@run-156","hlc_physical_ms":1789538306027,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"c2c50e78dada22de0fd6aefce9c6724c5d2eb4361c1f83d8ad7b47c3c8a1be9c","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2MCQ1ZAZHG0D16ZZQY36J5T","author":"exam:3@run-156","body":"examiner (task 3, card cells): writing `fleet/tests/test_sandbox_boot_card_cells.mjs` as a boot sim in the shape of the other sandbox-boot sims — shared helpers only, no sibling sim named.\n\nReading of the legs I am encoding:\n- (a) [M1] one boot on `DEFAULT_REPORT.replace('\"reviewVerdict\":\"approve\"', '\"reviewVerdict\":\"skipped-mutant-killed\"')`; the PR body's single `| 1 | ` line must EQUAL the Proof's verbatim row ending `| killed, reviewer skipped | green |`. Full-line equality, not containment, so every other cell is pinned too.\n- (b) [M2] two halves: the rig's shared default green boot (verdict `approve`, every `mutant_killed:true`) — cell is `killed`, body carries no `reviewer skipped`; and a third boot whose report carries `\"mutant_killed\":false` BESIDE `\"reviewVerdict\":\"skipped-mutant-killed\"` — cell is `SURVIVED`, body carries no `reviewer skipped`. Both halves are GREEN at BASE on purpose: they are M2's regression half, and the second is the one that fails a card keying on the verdict before the survivor check.\n- (c) [M3] the Proof's second `Run:` line run verbatim through bash (sed the card paragraph from the table line to `Residuals: <n> from review`, fold, grep `mutant.*skipped-mutant-killed.*killed, reviewer skipped`). Exits 1 at BASE — confirmed.\n\nThree boots and no more: the two new reports plus `greenAsync()`. Each fixture is built by `replace` with an assertion that the